d that the new notes would have investment\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [586, 175, 978, 253], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"yields of approximately 1.56 percent per annum if held for six months, 1.91 percent for one year, 2.10 percent for eighteen months, and 2.21 percent if held for the full two years to maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [586, 274, 982, 431], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"The accompanying table shows for the denomination of $1,000 the monthly tax-payment or redemption values and approximate investment yields. The official circular, No. 931, dated October 1, 1953, includes a table showing these data for each denomination, and gives the terms of the offering in full.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [335, 468, 766, 494], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"Treasury Savings Notes of Series C -- Tax-Payment or Redemption Values and Investment Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 509, 981, 573], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"The table below shows for each month from issue date to maturity date the amount of interest accrual, the principal amount with accrued interest added, for notes of the $1,000 denomination; the approximate investment yield on the par value from issue date to the 15th of each month following the issue date; and the approximate investment yield on the current redemption value from the 15th of the month indicated to the maturity date.\", \"des","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"{\"document\": {\"elements\": [{\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [0, 0, 1062, 1457], \"page_id\": 1}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [62, 1195, 929, 1286], \"page_id\": 3}], \"content\": \"UNITED STATES TREASURY DEPARTMENT OFFICE OF THE SECRETA