y impact the final result.\n\nI'll need to carefully convert the percentages to their decimal equivalents before performing the geometric mean calculation to ensure accuracy.\n\nBy converting each percentage to a decimal (dividing by 100), I can systematically multiply these values together. The calculation involves raising each decimal rate to the power of 1/n, where n represents the total number of rates.\n\nThe process involves multiplying 13 decimal values (converted from percentages), then taking the 14th root to find the geometric mean. I'll use a computational approach to verify the precise mathematical result.\n\nThe geometric mean calculation converts percentages to decimals, multiplies them together, and extracts the 14th root. This yields a decimal value of approximately 1.584%, which translates back to a percentage format.\n\nThe key steps involve precise decimal conversion, exponential manipulation, and careful root extraction to derive the final geometric mean percentage.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_85b8249e217241ba88cf1ad5","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Explore the resource files to understand the data structure\n- [x] Find weekly average discount rates for 91-day bills in September for 1953, 1954, 1955\n- [x] Extract Thursday rates for each week in September\n- [ ] Calculate geometric mean of all values\n- [ ] Round to nearest thousandths place\n- [ ] Write answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
